## Introduction

Integrating a point of sale (POS) terminal with Centrapay APIs allows merchants to accept payment via any Centrapay-enabled apps without installing additional POS hardware or software.

## Payment Flow

- [QR Code Flow](/guides/merchant-integration-qr-code-flow): the POS displays a QR code for the patron to scan with their Centrapay app.
- [Barcode Flow](/guides/merchant-integration-barcode-flow): the POS scans a barcode presented by the patron.

## Interface Guidelines

Use the [Centrapay Logos](/guides/centrapay-logos) when building the UI for Centrapay payments.

### Payment Option

Always display **Centrapay** as a payment option. Choose the **Centrapay logo** format that best suits the POS system's design. Use the [Centrapay brand orange](/guides/centrapay-logos#brand-colour) wherever possible.

![A POS payment screen with an orange Centrapay payment option button](/guideline/guideline-03.png)

### QR Code

The payment QR code screen must display the **Centrapay logo**, for example above or below the QR code, or in the centre of the QR code. The copy can be "**Scan to pay**" or "**Scan to pay with Centrapay**".

![A POS screen showing a Centrapay QR code with the Centrapay logo and Scan to pay with Centrapay copy](/guideline/guideline-04.png)
